# Ownership of the verification surface (principle 09). These paths decide what
# the repository checks and how, so changing one is authorizing a change to the
# rules themselves. With one maintainer, no review is required (GitHub does not
# count an author's own approval): this file declares the surface, the branch
# ruleset requires a pull request and the CI check, and the maintainer's merge is
# the authorization.
